     "title": "Write Your One-Page Plan Right Now",
     "content": "Do this before you close this lesson — not later today, not this weekend, now, while the five pillars are still fresh.\n\n1. **Obstacle audit.** Name your single most active obstacle from lesson seven and write the one countermeasure you commit to this week, in specific terms.\n\n2. **Quadrant target.** State your current primary quadrant honestly and your specific twelve-month target, with a number attached, not a vague direction.\n\n3. **Asset test.** Write one sentence defining the numeric test any asset must pass before you buy it, so future you has a rule to follow under pressure.\n\n4. **Protection trigger.** Name the specific event that will trigger a conversation with an attorney or CPA about forming a protective entity.\n\n5. **Deal pipeline.** Commit to a specific weekly number of opportunities you will review, and decide exactly where you will log every one you reject.\n\nThen do one more thing: put a **ninety-day review** on your actual calendar right now, today, to reread this one page and grade yourself honestly against all five lines. The plan only works if it is revisited, not just written once and quietly forgotten.",
